 :lesson/sections
 [{:section/type :accuracy-pointer
   :section/id 15
   :section/title "To Know a person or to know a fact"
   :section/body
   ["The Spanish language distinguishes between knowing people and places, Conocer, and knowing facts, saber."
    "One is to do with knowledge - saber And the other is to do with acquaintance - conocer If you go on to really develop your Spanish a day will come when they are immediately different to you."
    "For now we are going to use Conocer about knowing or being aquainted with people and places."
    "When you meet someone for the first time you can often use conocer"
    "For example Gusto en conocerle. A pleasure to meet you."
    "Voy a conocer a mi nieta en Enero. I am going to meet (for the first time) my granddaughter in January."]}
  {:section/type :communication-multiplied
   :section/id 15
   :section/title "We want to see them this weekend"
   :section/body
   ["Queremos verlos este fin de semana So far you have learned these structures Quiero verlo I want to see him Quiero verla I want to see her Quiere verme you want to see me Quiere vernos you want to see us Let's take it a step further and talk about seeing them"
    "Method 1 Los quiero ver them I want to see Los queremos ver them we want to see Or you can attach Lo to the Brick Verb."
    "Method 2 Quiero verlos I want to see them Queremos verlos we want to see them If you are talking about them and they are women, change los to las."
    "Method 1 Las quiero ver them I want to see (the girls or women) Las queremos ver them we want to see (the girls or women) Or you can attach Las to the Brick Verb."
    "Method 2 Quiero verlas I want to see them (the girls or women) Queremos verlas we want to see them (the girls or women) We'll continue using method 2, so you get the fastest Spanish integration."
    "If you are speaking about a mixed group of men and women use los."
    "Let's not analyze it too much. Instead here's a better idea, why don't you get a lot of practice right now. That way you can develop your \"sense\" of Spanish."]}]
